Article 3 (Methods of Prior Announcement of Legislation)
(1) When making a prior announcement of legislation, the chairperson shall publish the following matters in the National Assembly Bulletin or on the website of the National Assembly or the competent committee (hereinafter referred to as the "National Assembly or committee website"): Provided, That where the prior announcement is published in the National Assembly Bulletin, the full text of the bill (including a comparative table of provisions before and after amendment in the case of a bill partially amending an Act; hereinafter the same shall apply) may be omitted.
1. The proposer or submitter;
2. The purpose of legislation (meaning the reasons for proposing the bill);
3. The main contents;
4. The full text of the bill;
5. Cost-estimation materials and other matters under Article 79-2 of the Act;
6. The entity to which opinions are submitted and the period and method for submitting opinions.
(2) The chairperson may, within budgetary limits, place advertisements in newspapers, broadcasts, magazines, on the Internet or through other means concerning bills that need to be widely publicized, including bills containing matters with a significant impact on major national policies or the lives of citizens.
